## Goal
Perform principal component analysis (PCA) of RNA-seq samples based on gene-level count expression data, coloured by sample condition, to assess overall sample clustering, variance structure, and group separation between conditions.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | 01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_prepare_samplesheets | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. Load `01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv` to map each `sample_id` to its experimental `condition`.
2. Load the gene count matrix `02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv`, extracting numeric count columns corresponding to sample IDs and filtering out genes with zero counts across all samples.
3. Apply log2 transformation with a pseudocount of 1 (log2(counts + 1)) to normalize expression variance across samples.
4. Perform Principal Component Analysis (PCA) on transposed sample expression profiles using `scikit-learn` (`sklearn.decomposition.PCA(n_components=2)`) in the `gars-bio` conda environment.
5. Compute the percentage of variance explained by PC1 and PC2.
6. Export the sample projection table containing sample ID, PC1 coordinates, PC2 coordinates, and condition annotation to `results/pca_coordinates.csv`.
7. Generate a 2D scatter plot of PC1 versus PC2 using `matplotlib` in the `gars-bio` environment, coloured by condition, annotated with sample labels and explained variance ratios on axis titles, saving the figure to `results/pca_plot.png`.
8. All steps execute as a batch job via the configured workspace scheduler without modifying any upstream input files in place.

## Outputs
Types come from the closed vocabulary in _references/artifact_types.md.

| File | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| results/pca_coordinates.csv | table | Sample PCA coordinates (PC1, PC2) with condition metadata |
| results/pca_plot.png | figure | PCA scatter plot of samples coloured by condition |

## Execution
Runs: batch
Expected wall time: < 2 minutes; output size: < 2 MB.
